        "checkedAt": "2026-11-19T03:16:05.171Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E4",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Following our open beta , administrators can now deploy natural-language classification instructions at scale with two new capabilities designed to provide admins a better understanding of automated data classification for their files:",
        "sourceUrl": "https://workspaceupdates.googleblog.com/2026/11/gemini-powered-data-classification-in-Google-Drive-is-now-generally-available.html",
        "source": "Google Workspace Updates",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-17T22:00:35.941Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-19T03:16:05.171Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E5",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "By automating file identification and labeling across Drive, AI classification helps organizations enforce granular data loss prevention (DLP) policies at scale, establish retention rules, and utilize label metadata during audit investigations.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://workspaceupdates.googleblog.com/2026/11/gemini-powered-data-classification-in-Google-Drive-is-now-generally-available.html",
        "source": "Google Workspace Updates",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-17T22:00:35.941Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-19T03:16:05.171Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E6",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "This feature leverages Gemini models to apply data classification labels to files in Google Drive.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://workspaceupdates.googleblog.com/2026/11/gemini-powered-data-classification-in-Google-Drive-is-now-generally-available.html",
        "source": "Google Workspace Updates",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-17T22:00:35.941Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-19T03:16:05.171Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E7",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Previously, AI classification required admins to identify and manually label training files for the AI model to learn the types of data associated with each data classification level.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://workspaceupdates.googleblog.com/2026/11/gemini-powered-data-classification-in-Google-Drive-is-now-generally-available.html",
        "source": "Google Workspace Updates",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-17T22:00:35.941Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-19T03:16:05.171Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E8",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Model limits: Organizations are limited to 1 active Gemini instruction model, however, they can create up to 5 AI classification models in total (combining custom-trained ML models and Gemini instruction models).",
        "sourceUrl": "https://workspaceupdates.googleblog.com/2026/11/gemini-powered-data-classification-in-Google-Drive-is-now-generally-available.html",
        "source": "Google Workspace Updates",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-17T22:00:35.941Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-19T03:16:05.171Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E9",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Gemini classification will not overwrite labels manually applied, accepted, or modified by users, nor labels applied by data loss prevention (DLP) rules.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://workspaceupdates.googleblog.com/2026/11/gemini-powered-data-classification-in-Google-Drive-is-now-generally-available.html",
        "source": "Google Workspace Updates",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-17T22:00:35.941Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-19T03:16:05.171Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E10",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Data regions & privacy: Gemini-based AI classification respects your Google Workspace Data Regions settings.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://workspaceupdates.googleblog.com/2026/11/gemini-powered-data-classification-in-Google-Drive-is-now-generally-available.html",
        "source": "Google Workspace Updates",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-17T22:00:35.941Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-19T03:16:05.171Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E11",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Admins: For customers on a supported product license, the option for configuring Gemini-based AI classification instructions will appear in the Workspace Admin Console under the Data Classification option in the Security section (Security > Access and data control > Data class…",
        "sourceUrl": "https://workspaceupdates.googleblog.com/2026/11/gemini-powered-data-classification-in-Google-Drive-is-now-generally-available.html",
